  "summary": "This study fabricated LiF/HCl-etched Ti3C2Tx films, three Ti3C2Tx/PEDOT:PSS blend levels (P-50, P-100, and P-200), and their concentrated-H2SO4-treated counterparts, plus P-H and an rGO-film reference. Thus, ten distinct fabricated electrode materials were identified; rGO was the positive electrode of the asymmetric device, whereas P-H was a non-MXene three-electrode reference. Ti3C2Tx/P-100-H is the headline and best direct-measurement performer, reporting 1065 F cm\u22123 (286 F g\u22121) at 2 mV s\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4. Its reported BET area and Ti3C2Tx-layer spacing were 73.7 m2 g\u22121 and 15.1 \u00c5, respectively. Numerical capacitances for P-50, P-50-H, P-200, P-200-H, and Ti3C2Tx-H are not printed in the supplied main text; their performance appears only in cited supplementary figures."
}